    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d19">

                <pb facs="0015" n="9" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg9"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.24/55: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wright</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-07-06T13:00:00-05:00">July 6, 1939—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>71. Your circular telegram of June 27, 7 p.m. Secretary of State, as well as the
                    Secretary of National Defense and Colonel Batista<anchor n="6" xml:id="d19-f1"/>
                    <pb facs="0016" n="10" xml:id="pg10"/> to both of whom the Secretary of State
                    referred me and the latter of whom has been absent but whom I have now seen,
                    express themselves as wholly in sympathy with the purposes of the resolution,
                    the points of which as enumerated in the Department’s telegram I have discussed
                    with them in some detail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wright</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d19-f1" n="6" xml:id="d19-f1-content">
                <p>Fulgencia Batista, Chief of Staff, Cuban Army.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
